c =========================================================================
c PROFILE 2 - POST-MI ELDERLY + CHRONIC PAIN + DEPRESSION (30-qubit CNF)
c =========================================================================
c
c Patient archetype: Mrs S, 70 years old, recent ST-elevation MI (3 mo
c post-revascularization), HFrEF EF=38%, hypertension, diabetic peripheral
c neuropathy, post-MI major depression, primary hypothyroidism.
c
c Epidemiology backing:
c   - 20-30% of post-MI patients develop major depression
c     (Glassman AH et al. SADHART JAMA 2002;288:701-9)
c   - Sertraline is the first-line SSRI post-MI (FDA-approved indication,
c     SADHART safety/efficacy data)
c   - Diabetic peripheral neuropathy affects ~50% of T2DM with >10 yr
c     duration (Pop-Busui R. Diabetes Care 2017;40:136-54)
c   - Pregabalin FDA-approved for DPNP (FDA label 2004)
c
c Format   : DIMACS WCNF for qaoa_wcnf.py
c Encoding : CJ2 (Ansotegui & Levy 2024; Rodriguez Farres ICCS 2024)
c Qubits   : 30  (12 drug variables + 18 ternary-syndrome clauses)
c
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c DRUG POOL (all FDA-approved; HODDI-verified)
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c   x1   Acetylsalicylic acid DB00945  B01AC   Antiplatelet (8,006)
c                                                ACC/AHA Class I post-MI
c   x2   Clopidogrel          DB00758  B01AC   P2Y12 antagonist (1,693)
c                                                CURE/AUGUSTUS DAPT
c   x3   Atorvastatin         DB01076  C10AA   HMG-CoA (5,222)
c                                                ACC/AHA Class I post-MI
c   x4   Metoprolol           DB00264  C07AB   β-blocker (4,332)
c                                                ACC/AHA Class I post-MI
c   x5   Lisinopril           DB00722  C09AA   ACEi (4,175)
c                                                ACC/AHA Class I HF post-MI
c   x6   Hydrochlorothiazide  DB00999  C03AA   Thiazide (3,961)
c                                                HTN management
c   x7   Furosemide           DB00695  C03CA   Loop diuretic (3,175)
c                                                HF symptom mgmt
c   x8   Pantoprazole         DB00213  A02BC   PPI (3,578)
c                                                DAPT gastroprotection
c   x9   Omeprazole           DB00338  A02BC   PPI alternative (4,652)
c   x10  Sertraline           DB01104  N06AB   SSRI (2,890)
c                                                SADHART JAMA 2002 post-MI MDD
c   x11  Pregabalin           DB00230  N02BF   Gabapentinoid (4,197)
c                                                FDA-approved DPNP
c   x12  Levothyroxine        DB00451  H03AA   Thyroid hormone (8,837)
c                                                Hypothyroidism (common >=65)
c
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c AVOIDANCE CLAUSES (c01-c06) - HODDI HIGHER-ORDER SIGNALS + ACC/AHA
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c
c c01 (x1=ASA + x4=Meto + x11=Pregabalin -> Wound / bleeding complication)
c   HODDI signal: PRR=499.2 (95% CI 257.1-969.3), a=4 cases,
c                  p_fisher=6.4e-11, IC=3.15 (Bonferroni-passing)
c   Strongest higher-order signal in profile - established bleeding
c   amplification: ASA antiplatelet + βB-induced bradycardia
c   (fall predisposition) + pregabalin-related dizziness/sedation
c   (Beers 2023 caution: pregabalin in elderly)
c   Weight: 100 (Tier A)
c
c c02 (x1=ASA + x4=Meto + x8=Pantoprazole -> Wound)
c   HODDI signal: PRR=134.4 (95% CI 53.7-336.3), a=4, p_fisher=2.7e-08
c   Same bleeding mechanism (ASA antiplatelet effect)
c   Pantoprazole present as DAPT gastroprotection - signal captures
c   "patient on full post-MI regimen has elevated wound/bleed risk"
c   Weight: 100 (Tier A)
c
c c03 (x1=ASA + x4=Meto + x8=Pantoprazole -> Impaired healing)
c   HODDI signal: PRR=107.2, a=3, p_fisher=3.3e-06
c   ASA impairs platelet-mediated wound healing
c   Weight: 50 (Tier B)
c
c c04 (x1=ASA + x3=Atorvastatin + x7=Furosemide -> Discomfort)
c   HODDI signal: PRR=44.8, a=3, p_fisher=4.4e-05
c   Plausible mechanism: ASA-induced GI discomfort + statin myalgia +
c   furosemide volume contraction/cramping
c   Weight: 30 (Tier C - vague AE term)
c
c c05 (x1=ASA + x3=Atorvastatin + x6=HCTZ -> General deterioration)
c   HODDI signal: PRR=34.9 (95% CI 14.4-84.6), a=4, p_fisher=5.0e-06
c   Composite elderly polypharmacy decompensation signal
c   Weight: 30
c
c c06 (x1=ASA + x3=Atorvastatin + x4=Metoprolol -> Hepatic enzymes ↑)
c   HODDI signal: PRR=31.1 (95% CI 12.1-79.7), a=4, p_fisher=9.3e-06
c   Statin hepatotoxicity (FDA label Atorvastatin) amplified by
c   βB cardiovascular load + ASA
c   Weight: 50 (Tier B)
c
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c POSITIVE GUIDELINE CLAUSES (c07-c18)
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c
c c07 (x1 v x2 v x3): DAPT + statin post-MI core
c   ACC/AHA STEMI/NSTEMI Class I: aspirin + P2Y12 inhibitor (DAPT) +
c   statin as core post-MI medical therapy
c   (CURE NEJM 2001, TRITON NEJM 2007, AUGUSTUS NEJM 2019)
c   Weight: 30 (Class I)
c
c c08 (x4 v x5 v x3): Post-MI medical backbone
c   ACC/AHA Class I: β-blocker + ACEi + statin for HFrEF post-MI
c   (SAVE NEJM 1992, MERIT-HF Lancet 1999)
c   Weight: 30
c
c c09 (x5 v x4 v x7): HF management triad
c   ACEi/ARB + β-blocker + loop diuretic (HFrEF, AHA 2022)
c   Weight: 30
c
c c10 (x5 v x6 v x4): Hypertension control
c   ACEi + thiazide + β-blocker - typical HTN combination
c   (ALLHAT JAMA 2002; JNC 8 / 2017 ACC/AHA HTN Guideline)
c   Weight: 30
c
c c11 (x8 v x9 v x1): PPI gastroprotection with DAPT
c   ACC/AHA + ACG Class I: PPI when ASA or DAPT used in patients
c   with bleeding risk factors
c   (Bhatt DL et al. JACC 2008;52:1502)
c   Weight: 30
c
c c12 (x10 v x11 v x4): Post-MI psychiatric/neuropathic management
c   AHA + APA: SSRI for post-MI depression (Glassman SADHART);
c   Pregabalin for neuropathic pain (FDA-approved DPNP)
c   Weight: 30
c
c c13 (x12 v x10 v x3): Endocrine + mood + lipid management
c   Levothyroxine for hypothyroidism (universal in elderly);
c   SSRI for MDD; statin for atherosclerosis
c   Weight: 15 (Class IIa multi-system)
c
c c14 (x1 v x4 v x5): Post-MI Class I trifecta
c   Aspirin + β-blocker + ACEi - cited together in every ACC/AHA
c   post-MI quality-of-care metric
c   Weight: 15
c
c c15 (x6 v x7 v x5): Volume/RAAS management for HFrEF
c   Loop+thiazide+ACEi for diuretic-RAAS combination
c   Weight: 15
c
c c16 (x8 v x9 v x11): GI + neuropathy management
c   PPI for gastroprotection + pregabalin for DPNP (common elderly stack)
c   Weight: 15
c
c c17 (x3 v x10 v x12): Long-term elderly maintenance bundle
c   Statin + SSRI + levothyroxine as chronic disease control regimen
c   Weight: 15
c
c c18 (x2 v x3 v x4): Cardiac quality-of-care
c   Clopidogrel + statin + β-blocker as performance measure trio
c   Weight: 15
c
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c WEIGHT TOTAL
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c   Tier A:    c01, c02                    = 200
c   Tier B:    c03, c06                    = 100
c   Tier C:    c04, c05                    =  60
c   Class I:   c07,c08,c09,c10,c11,c12     = 180
c   Class IIa: c13,c14,c15,c16,c17,c18     =  90
c   TOTAL = 630
c
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c REFERENCES
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c   Glassman AH et al. SADHART JAMA 2002;288:701-9 (sertraline post-MI)
c   Pop-Busui R et al. Diabetes Care 2017;40:136-54 (DPNP epidemiology)
c   ACC/AHA STEMI Guideline: O'Gara PT et al. JACC 2013;61:e78
c   ACC/AHA NSTEMI Guideline: Amsterdam EA et al. Circulation 2014
c   CURE Trial: NEJM 2001;345:494 (clopidogrel post-MI)
c   AUGUSTUS Trial: Lopes RD et al. NEJM 2019;380:1509
c   SAVE Trial: Pfeffer MA et al. NEJM 1992;327:669 (captopril post-MI)
c   MERIT-HF: Lancet 1999;353:2001 (metoprolol succinate HFrEF)
c   2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA HF Guideline (Heidenreich et al.)
c   2017 ACC/AHA HTN Guideline (Whelton et al.)
c   ALLHAT: JAMA 2002;288:2981
c   Bhatt DL et al. JACC 2008;52:1502 (PPI with DAPT)
c   AGS Beers Criteria 2023
c   FDA Labels: Aspirin, Clopidogrel, Atorvastatin, Metoprolol,
c     Lisinopril, Pantoprazole, Sertraline, Pregabalin (DailyMed)
c   HODDI dataset: arXiv:2502.06274
c   DDInter 2.0: Nucleic Acids Res 2025;53(D1):D1356
c
c =========================================================================
p wcnf 12 18 101
100 -1 -4 -11 0   c c01  ASA+Meto+Pregab -> Wound (HODDI Tier A PRR=499)
100 -1 -4 -8 0    c c02  ASA+Meto+Panto -> Wound (Tier A PRR=134)
 50 -1 -4 -8 0    c c03  ASA+Meto+Panto -> Impaired healing
 30 -1 -3 -7 0    c c04  ASA+Atorv+Furo -> Discomfort
 30 -1 -3 -6 0    c c05  ASA+Atorv+HCTZ -> General deterioration
 50 -1 -3 -4 0    c c06  ASA+Atorv+Meto -> Hepatic enzymes increased
 30  1  2  3 0    c c07  DAPT+statin post-MI core (ACC/AHA Class I)
 30  4  5  3 0    c c08  Post-MI medical backbone (BB+ACEi+statin)
 30  5  4  7 0    c c09  HFrEF management triad
 30  5  6  4 0    c c10  HTN combination control
 30  8  9  1 0    c c11  PPI w/ DAPT gastroprotection (ACC/AHA Class I)
 30  10 11 4 0    c c12  Post-MI MDD + DPNP management
 15  12 10 3 0    c c13  Endocrine + mood + lipid
 15  1  4  5 0    c c14  Post-MI Class I trifecta
 15  6  7  5 0    c c15  Volume/RAAS HFrEF mgmt
 15  8  9  11 0   c c16  GI + neuropathy mgmt
 15  3  10 12 0   c c17  Elderly maintenance bundle
 15  2  3  4 0    c c18  Cardiac performance measure trio
